# the exit instead -- one transaction from the address the swap memo names in
# public, straight to the operator's destination.
#
# So the stall clock asks "has anything NEW arrived recently?" and restarts on
# every real arrival, which is what lets N chunks land over an afternoon
# without anyone having to guess N * (swap settle time) in advance. The
# absolute cap is the backstop that keeps a run from waiting forever when a
# chunk is never sent at all.
